{
  "id": "report-short-3-cron-en",
  "title": "200 people request the same report: do you generate it 200 times?",
  "lang": "en",
  "pack": "tech",
  "theme": "light",
  "board": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "frontend",
        "label": "Frontend",
        "icon": "client",
        "row": 0,
        "col": 0,
        "sub": "web app"
      },
      {
        "id": "api",
        "label": "Backend",
        "icon": "api",
        "row": 0,
        "col": 1,
        "sub": "REST API"
      },
      {
        "id": "queue",
        "label": "Queue",
        "icon": "queue",
        "row": 1,
        "col": 1,
        "sub": "pending jobs"
      },
      {
        "id": "db",
        "label": "Database",
        "icon": "db",
        "row": 1,
        "col": 2,
        "sub": "sales"
      },
      {
        "id": "store",
        "label": "S3",
        "icon": "storage",
        "row": 2,
        "col": 0,
        "sub": "files"
      },
      {
        "id": "worker",
        "label": "Worker",
        "icon": "worker",
        "row": 2,
        "col": 1,
        "sub": "also backend"
      },
      {
        "id": "cron",
        "label": "Cron",
        "icon": "scheduler",
        "row": 2,
        "col": 2,
        "sub": "every night"
      }
    ],
    "edges": [
      {
        "from": "frontend",
        "to": "api"
      },
      {
        "from": "api",
        "to": "queue"
      },
      {
        "from": "queue",
        "to": "worker"
      },
      {
        "from": "worker",
        "to": "db"
      },
      {
        "from": "worker",
        "to": "store"
      },
      {
        "from": "store",
        "to": "frontend",
        "dashed": true
      },
      {
        "from": "cron",
        "to": "worker"
      }
    ]
  },
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "tag": "System design",
      "heading": "*200* people request the same report",
      "narration": "Monday, nine a.m.: two hundred people request the same sales report, and it takes minutes to generate. Do you generate it two hundred times?",
      "beats": [
        {
          "text": "×200",
          "icon": "users",
          "at": "two hundred people"
        },
        {
          "text": "Report",
          "icon": "file",
          "at": "the same sales report"
        },
        {
          "text": "Minutes",
          "icon": "scheduler",
          "at": "takes minutes",
          "sfx": "clock"
        },
        {
          "text": "?",
          "at": "Do you generate"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "Today's design",
      "narration": "You already have a queue and a worker: each request is queued, and the worker builds it separately and leaves it in S3. With few requests, it works perfectly.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "You already have",
          "show": [
            "frontend",
            "api",
            "queue",
            "worker",
            "db",
            "store"
          ],
          "camera": []
        },
        {
          "at": "each request is queued",
          "packet": {
            "from": "api",
            "to": "queue",
            "label": "job",
            "color": "yellow"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "builds it separately",
          "packet": {
            "from": "queue",
            "to": "worker",
            "label": "job",
            "color": "yellow"
          },
          "status": {
            "worker": "busy"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "leaves it in",
          "packet": {
            "from": "worker",
            "to": "store",
            "label": "report.csv",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "worker": "ok",
            "store": "ok"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "works perfectly",
          "note": {
            "text": "Few requests: *it works*",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "Its limit",
      "narration": "But two hundred identical requests arrive: the same heavy work two hundred times. The queue fills up and the database suffers. All for two hundred identical files.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "two hundred identical requests",
          "status": {
            "worker": "idle",
            "store": "idle"
          },
          "packet": {
            "from": "frontend",
            "to": "api",
            "label": "×200",
            "color": "orange"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "two hundred times",
          "packet": {
            "from": "api",
            "to": "queue",
            "label": "×200",
            "color": "orange"
          },
          "status": {
            "queue": "warn",
            "worker": "busy"
          },
          "note": {
            "text": "200 identical requests = *200 × the work*",
            "tone": "warn"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "queue fills up",
          "status": {
            "queue": "error"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "database suffers",
          "status": {
            "db": "error"
          },
          "sfx": "alarm"
        },
        {
          "at": "identical files",
          "focus": [
            "store"
          ],
          "note": {
            "text": "Same result: *why repeat it?*",
            "tone": "bad"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "Generate it once",
      "narration": "Instead, generate it just once. A cron job, which is a scheduled task, builds it every night, when almost nobody is using the system, and leaves it in S3.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "generate it just once",
          "status": {
            "queue": "idle",
            "db": "idle",
            "worker": "idle"
          },
          "focus": []
        },
        {
          "at": "A cron job",
          "show": [
            "cron"
          ],
          "focus": [
            "cron",
            "worker"
          ],
          "note": {
            "text": "Cron = *a scheduled task*",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "every night",
          "packet": {
            "from": "cron",
            "to": "worker",
            "label": "00:00",
            "color": "gray"
          },
          "status": {
            "worker": "busy"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "leaves it in",
          "packet": {
            "from": "worker",
            "to": "store",
            "label": "report.csv",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "worker": "ok",
            "store": "ok"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "board",
      "title": "Everyone, instantly",
      "narration": "On Monday, everyone downloads it instantly, and the queue isn't needed for this anymore. Careful: if each user wants different filters, you're back to the queue.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": "everyone downloads it",
          "focus": [
            "store",
            "frontend"
          ],
          "packet": {
            "from": "store",
            "to": "frontend",
            "label": "download",
            "color": "green"
          },
          "status": {
            "frontend": "ok"
          },
          "sfx": "success"
        },
        {
          "at": "isn't needed",
          "hide": [
            "queue"
          ],
          "focus": [],
          "camera": [],
          "note": {
            "text": "*Once* for everyone",
            "tone": "good"
          }
        },
        {
          "at": "different filters",
          "note": {
            "text": "Different filters → *back to the queue*",
            "tone": "info"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "summary",
      "title": "Don't repeat it",
      "narration": "If everyone wants the same thing, don't repeat it: precompute it. What other app do you think does this? The full design is on the channel.",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Same for everyone → *precompute*",
          "at": "If everyone wants"
        },
        {
          "text": "Different for each → *queue + worker*",
          "at": "precompute it"
        }
      ],
      "cta": "Full video on the channel ▶"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Precomputing fits when the result is the same for everyone and can be a few hours old; if each user needs up-to-the-minute data or their own filters, you go back to queue + worker.",
    "A middle ground: deduplicate identical requests in the queue (one key per report) and serve the same file to everyone who asked, or cache the result with a TTL.",
    "Cron can be a Linux cron job, your cloud provider's scheduler (EventBridge Scheduler, Cloud Scheduler) or your framework's scheduler."
  ],
  "publish": {
    "titles": [
      "200 People Request the Same Report: Do You Generate It 200 Times?",
      "Precompute With a Cron Job: Save Your Database"
    ],
    "description": "If everyone asks for the same heavy result, don't build it once per request: prepare it overnight with a cron job and serve it instantly.",
    "extra": [
      "🎬 The full video (from a simple API to a queue, a worker and a cron job) is on the channel."
    ],
    "comment": "What other app do you think precomputes like this?",
    "hashtags": [
      "systemdesign",
      "backend",
      "programming"
    ]
  },
  "thumbnail": {
    "text": "Generate it *200 times*?",
    "kicker": "System design",
    "icons": [
      {
        "icon": "users"
      },
      {
        "icon": "file"
      }
    ]
  }
}